  ('38987832-a8b6-5dfa-b628-54d30e77c7ef', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-argument-writing'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Which revision of sentence (11) best keeps a formal style and an objective tone?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Honestly, coaches should kind of just get over it and follow the new rules.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-informal-tone"},{"text":"Coaches who disagree simply do not understand how the game of baseball works.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dismissive-tone"},{"text":"Although coaches' concerns are reasonable, the Carroway results suggest limits need not make games less fair.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Coaches have many opinions, and every opinion matters a great deal in a debate.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-wording"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Although coaches' concerns are reasonable, the Carroway results suggest limits need not make games less fair.$q$, $q$The correct revision respects the coaches' view while pointing to the evidence in sentences (9) and (10). The first choice still attacks the coaches instead of answering their reasoning.$q$, 'draft', '8bc39fcc-09ec-5061-a577-6aac479d141c')
