   $q$Read the sentence: "The octopus changed the color of its skin; within a few seconds." Why is the semicolon incorrect?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A semicolon can never appear in a sentence about animals.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-rule"},{"text":"\"Within a few seconds\" is a phrase, not an independent clause.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The semicolon should come before \"changed\" instead.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-misplaced"},{"text":"A semicolon must always be followed by a capital letter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"capital-after-semicolon"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Within a few seconds" is a phrase, not an independent clause.$q$, $q$A semicolon needs an independent clause on both sides, and "within a few seconds" has no subject or verb, so the semicolon should be removed. Words after a semicolon are not capitalized unless they are proper nouns, so the capital-letter choice states a false rule.$q$, 'draft', null)
