   $q$Read the sentence: "The forecast called for heavy rain ___ the regatta ___ went on as planned." Which pair of choices correctly fills the two blanks?$q$, $q$[{"text":"(1) , (2) , however,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-with-adverb"},{"text":"(1) ; (2) however","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-commas-around-interrupter"},{"text":"(1) , however (2) ;","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-misplaced"},{"text":"(1) ; (2) , however,","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$(1) ; (2) , however,$q$, $q$The two independent clauses need a semicolon between them, and "however" interrupts the second clause, so commas set it off on both sides. Using only a comma at the first blank creates a comma splice even when "however" appears later.$q$, 'draft', null)
