   $q$Read the sentence: "The sailing club offered three beginner classes: Knot Tying, Reading the Wind, and Docking." The class names are not official titles. Which revision uses capitalization correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The sailing club offered three beginner classes: knot tying, reading the wind, and docking.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The Sailing Club offered three beginner classes: knot tying, reading the wind, and docking.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"capitalizes-common-nouns"},{"text":"The sailing club offered three beginner classes: Knot tying, reading the wind, and docking.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"capital-after-colon-list"},{"text":"The sailing club offered three beginner classes: Knot Tying, Reading The Wind, and Docking.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"capitalizes-common-nouns"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The sailing club offered three beginner classes: knot tying, reading the wind, and docking.$q$, $q$Items in a list after a colon are not capitalized unless they are proper nouns, so "knot tying, reading the wind, and docking" stays lowercase. Capitalizing only the first item treats the list as if it were a new sentence, which it is not.$q$, 'draft', null)
