   $q$Read the sentence: "The museum guide ended the tour with a simple reminder: ___" Which choice correctly completes the sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Every map leaves something out\".","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"period-outside-quotes"},{"text":"Every map leaves something out.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-quotation-marks"},{"text":"\"Every map leaves something out.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"every map leaves something out.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"lowercase-quoted-sentence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Every map leaves something out."$q$, $q$When a colon introduces a quoted complete sentence, the quotation begins with a capital letter, and in American usage the period goes inside the closing quotation mark. The lowercase "every" incorrectly treats the quoted sentence as a fragment.$q$, 'draft', null)
