   $q$Which sentence about a fundraiser is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The band sold 300 tickets for the concert nevertheless, the fundraiser fell short of its goal.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"run-on-sentence"},{"text":"The band sold 300 tickets for the concert, nevertheless, the fundraiser fell short of its goal.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-with-adverb"},{"text":"The band sold 300 tickets; for the concert, nevertheless the fundraiser fell short of its goal.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-misplaced"},{"text":"The band sold 300 tickets for the concert; nevertheless, the fundraiser fell short of its goal.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The band sold 300 tickets for the concert; nevertheless, the fundraiser fell short of its goal.$q$, $q$"Nevertheless" is a conjunctive adverb linking two independent clauses, so it needs a semicolon before it and a comma after it. The first choice uses only commas, which leaves a comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
