   $q$Read the sentence: "The north trail was closed for repairs the east trail was flooded only the river path remained open." Which revision is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The north trail was closed; for repairs the east trail was flooded; only the river path remained open.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-misplaced"},{"text":"The north trail was closed for repairs, the east trail was flooded, only the river path remained open.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice"},{"text":"The north trail was closed for repairs; the east trail was flooded, only the river path remained open.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice"},{"text":"The north trail was closed for repairs; the east trail was flooded; only the river path remained open.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The north trail was closed for repairs; the east trail was flooded; only the river path remained open.$q$, $q$The sentence contains three closely related independent clauses, and semicolons can link all three. The third choice fixes only the first break and leaves a comma splice between the second and third clauses.$q$, 'draft', null)
