  ('27673ed1-558c-5e63-955b-3941f094d802', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-capitalization-punctuation'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which sentence about a quilting exhibit uses a semicolon correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The quilts were sewn by hand; which took the guild nearly two years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-before-dependent-clause"},{"text":"Each quilt in the exhibit told a family story; one showed a grandmother's journey across three countries.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The guild finished the last quilt in March; because the exhibit opened in April.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-before-dependent-clause"},{"text":"The guild displayed quilts made of; cotton, wool, and silk.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-misplaced"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Each quilt in the exhibit told a family story; one showed a grandmother's journey across three countries.$q$, $q$Only the third choice has an independent clause on each side of the semicolon, and the second clause gives an example of the first. In the other choices, the semicolon comes before a dependent clause ("which took," "because the exhibit") or splits a preposition from its objects.$q$, 'draft', null)
