   $q$Read the sentence: "___ the forecast called for sunshine, the soccer match was postponed by a sudden storm." Which choice best completes the adverbial clause to show the intended meaning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"So that","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"shows-purpose-not-contrast"},{"text":"Because","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"shows-cause-not-contrast"},{"text":"Since","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"shows-cause-not-contrast"},{"text":"Although","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Although$q$, $q$A sunny forecast and a storm that postponed the match are in contrast, so "Although" is the right subordinating conjunction. "Because" would claim the sunny forecast caused the postponement, which is illogical.$q$, 'draft', null)
