  ('58e34f4c-3fc0-5646-99be-c529a57c3867', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-grammar-usage'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Read the sentence: "Learning to read music is as important as ___ the scales on the piano." Which choice completes the sentence with parallel structure?$q$, $q$[{"text":"learning","is_correct":true},{"text":"to learn","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"infinitive-breaks-parallel"},{"text":"you learn","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"clause-breaks-parallel"},{"text":"learned","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-verb-form"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$learning$q$, $q$The comparison begins with the gerund "Learning," so the second half should also use a gerund: "learning the scales." "To learn" is an infinitive, which does not match the first item.$q$, 'draft', null)
