  ('8844cef7-9d3b-54cd-a48f-8deddc7b6072', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-grammar-usage'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentence: "Her notebook open on the desk, Priya sketched the veins of the maple leaf." What kind of phrase is "Her notebook open on the desk"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"a dependent clause","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"phrase-called-clause"},{"text":"a prepositional phrase","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-absolute-prepositional"},{"text":"a participial phrase","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-absolute-participial"},{"text":"an absolute phrase","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$an absolute phrase$q$, $q$The phrase is a noun ("notebook") plus a modifier ("open on the desk") with no full verb, and it adds a detail about the whole scene, which makes it an absolute phrase. A participial phrase would begin with a participle, not with a noun and its own modifier.$q$, 'draft', null)
