  ('a16690a5-bb5b-55ac-ae7c-a17a977e5175', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-grammar-usage'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentence: "The volunteers spent Saturday painting fences, repairing benches, and they planted tulip bulbs along the path." Which revision corrects the faulty parallel structure?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The volunteers spent Saturday to paint fences, repairing benches, and planting tulip bulbs along the path.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"infinitive-breaks-parallel"},{"text":"The volunteers spent Saturday painting fences, benches repaired, and planting tulip bulbs along the path.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"noun-phrase-breaks-parallel"},{"text":"The volunteers spent Saturday painting fences, repairing benches, and had planted tulip bulbs along the path.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"verb-breaks-parallel"},{"text":"The volunteers spent Saturday painting fences, repairing benches, and planting tulip bulbs along the path.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The volunteers spent Saturday painting fences, repairing benches, and planting tulip bulbs along the path.$q$, $q$All three activities now use the same "ing" form: "painting," "repairing," and "planting." The other revisions still mix forms, such as "to paint" or "had planted," with the gerund phrases.$q$, 'draft', null)
