  ('4903ec36-946d-5eeb-adb0-9c5a5cd546c2', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-grammar-usage'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentence: "The museum guide explained that the fossil was older than the mountains around it." How does the clause "that the fossil was older than the mountains around it" function?$q$, $q$[{"text":"as a relative clause modifying \"guide\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-relative-noun-clause"},{"text":"as an independent clause joined to the first one","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-subordinator"},{"text":"as a noun clause serving as the direct object of \"explained\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"as an adverbial clause telling why the guide explained","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-noun-adverbial-clause"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$as a noun clause serving as the direct object of "explained"$q$, $q$The clause answers "Explained what?" so it is a noun clause acting as the direct object. It does not describe the guide, so it is not a relative clause, even though it begins with "that."$q$, 'draft', null)
