insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('978d4ab1-d887-5473-a5fa-2e057905f158', 'wg10-informative-writing-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-informative-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$How Wheelchair Basketball Works$q$, $q$(1) Wheelchair basketball is played on a standard court with a regulation hoop, but every athlete competes from a specially designed sports chair. (2) The sport began in the 1940s as a form of physical rehabilitation and has since grown into an international competition. (3) In Kestrel County, a youth league founded in 2015 now includes eight teams.

(4) Sports chairs differ from everyday wheelchairs in several ways. (5) Their wheels tilt inward at the top, an angle called camber, which makes the chair more stable during sharp turns. (6) A small extra wheel at the back keeps the chair from tipping over when a player leans back to shoot.

(7) The rules are similar to those of standard basketball, with a few important changes. (8) A player may push the wheels twice while holding the ball but then must dribble, pass or shoot. (9) Each player receives a classification score from 1.0 to 4.5 based on physical function, and the five players on the court together may not exceed 14 points. (10) This system ensures that every team includes athletes with a range of abilities.

(11) The jerseys in the Kestrel County league are blue and gold.

(12) That is everything about wheelchair basketball.$q$, 'draft')
