  ('bd51c100-5ab9-52d1-a888-ef6887c04ab2', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-narrative-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which sentence, added after sentence 18, would best conclude the narrative with a reflection that connects to earlier events?$q$, $q$[{"text":"I replaced the A string the next morning and practiced my scales for an hour.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flat-ending-no-reflection"},{"text":"Cello strings can break when they get old or when the weather turns dry and cold.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"},{"text":"Maybe Ms. Varga was right: Kofi had not heard a mistake, only a cello answering the orchestra the best way it could.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The winter concert also included a choir and a short jazz band set after the intermission.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Maybe Ms. Varga was right: Kofi had not heard a mistake, only a cello answering the orchestra the best way it could.$q$, $q$The correct choice links Kofi's reaction to Ms. Varga's advice in sentence 6 and shows the narrator rethinking the doubt in sentence 7. The new string choice only reports a later action.$q$, 'draft', '037409a3-bb8c-5ebc-8dbe-cacefb12944c')
