   $q$The writer wants to add a concluding sentence after sentence 13. Which choice best concludes the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Railroads also changed how mail, newspapers, and fresh food traveled between distant cities.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"Some of the old station clocks from that era are now displayed in museums across the country.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"A system invented to keep trains on schedule had quietly become the way an entire nation measured its days.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Therefore, every town should have refused to change its clocks until the government acted.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-passage"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A system invented to keep trains on schedule had quietly become the way an entire nation measured its days.$q$, $q$The correct choice ties together the whole passage, from the railroads' problem to the nation's adoption of the zones. The sentence about other things railroads changed is tempting because it mentions railroads, but it opens a new topic instead of closing the one the passage developed.$q$, 'draft', '0643af17-a9ea-542d-972a-1724340a6254')
