  ('8dcf80dc-c168-5412-97ad-71ab67233e6a', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence at the end of the second paragraph that leads into the third. Which choice does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Every tree in every forest is therefore connected to every other tree.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Phosphorus is one of the most important nutrients for healthy plant growth.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Fungi also produce mushrooms, which many forest animals eat.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"How much the trees actually share through this network, however, is still an open question.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$How much the trees actually share through this network, however, is still an open question.$q$, $q$The correct choice builds on the idea of a network in sentence 7 and raises the question that the research in paragraph 3 tries to answer. The claim that every tree is connected overstates sentence 7, which says only that some neighboring trees can be linked.$q$, 'draft', '826efc48-60bf-59cd-8a07-6ad490e43439')
