insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('698d55f3-4cc1-5f96-afd0-e33dddc47f28', 'wg10-paragraph-transitions-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-paragraph-transitions'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Students on the Air$q$, $q$(1) Every weekday morning at seven, students at Riverside High run a small radio station that broadcasts to the surrounding neighborhood. (2) The station began six years ago as a single microphone in a storage closet, and it now operates from a converted classroom with a soundproof booth. (3) Students write the scripts, operate the mixing board, and host every program. (4) ____ the station has become a training ground for students interested in journalism, music, and engineering.

(5) The morning show follows a fixed structure that listeners have come to expect. (6) It opens with local weather and traffic reports, which students gather by calling the city information line. (7) ____, a different student reads short community announcements, such as library events or road closures. (8) The final segment features an interview with a neighbor, from a bakery owner to a retired bus driver. (9) Many radios from the early twentieth century were built inside heavy wooden cabinets.

(10) Running a station has taught the students lessons that reach beyond broadcasting. (11) When a guest cancels at the last minute, the hosts must fill the time without sounding unprepared. (12) When equipment fails, the student engineers must solve the problem quickly while the station stays on the air. (13) ____, the students learn to stay calm under pressure, a skill that will serve them in almost any career.$q$, 'draft')
