  ('d003b549-3ac3-5d3c-9465-08952a8106ee', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read: "(1) A solar oven is a box lined with reflective panels that concentrate sunlight onto a dark pot. (2) The dark pot absorbs the light and turns it into heat, while a clear lid keeps that heat inside. (3) On a sunny day, a well-built solar oven can become hot enough to bake bread or cook rice." Which sentence would best conclude this paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"For this reason, solar ovens are completely useless and should never be used at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-paragraph"},{"text":"Some solar ovens are painted bright colors on the outside so they are easy to spot.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Because it needs no fuel beyond sunlight, a solar oven offers a practical way to cook where firewood or electricity is scarce.","is_correct":true},{"text":"People in many cultures have cooked food over open fires for thousands of years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because it needs no fuel beyond sunlight, a solar oven offers a practical way to cook where firewood or electricity is scarce.$q$, $q$The correct choice draws a conclusion from the paragraph's explanation of how the oven works and why that matters. The sentence about open fires is tempting because it mentions cooking, but it shifts to a new subject instead of closing the one the paragraph built.$q$, 'draft', null)
