  ('c6784cf2-3ca1-5b32-8e3f-24452b0feb2c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read: "(1) In tournament chess, each player has a limited amount of time for the whole game. (2) A chess clock has two faces, one for each player, and only one clock runs at a time. (3) After moving, a player presses a button that stops that player's clock and starts the opponent's. (4) The knight is the only chess piece that can jump over other pieces. (5) If a player's time runs out, that player usually loses, no matter how strong the position on the board." Which sentence does not belong?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sentence 4","is_correct":true},{"text":"Sentence 3","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-supporting-detail"},{"text":"Sentence 5","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-supporting-detail"},{"text":"Sentence 2","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-key-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sentence 4$q$, $q$The paragraph explains how time limits and chess clocks work, and the way a knight moves has nothing to do with timing. Sentence 5 belongs because it explains what happens when a player's time runs out.$q$, 'draft', null)
