   $q$A student writes in a science summary: "Migrating geese fly in a V shape, which is awesome because it saves energy." Which revision keeps an objective tone?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Migrating geese fly in a V shape, which wastes energy.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-meaning"},{"text":"Migrating geese fly in an amazing V shape that saves energy.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"emotional-language"},{"text":"Migrating geese fly in a cool V shape, which saves energy.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-word"},{"text":"Migrating geese fly in a V shape, which saves energy.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Migrating geese fly in a V shape, which saves energy.$q$, $q$Removing "awesome" leaves the fact stated neutrally. Replacing it with "amazing" or "cool" still inserts the writer's feelings into a science summary.$q$, 'draft', null)
