   $q$Read the sentence: "The orchard grows twelve kinds of apples, the most popular is a tart green variety." Which revision does NOT correct the error?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The orchard grows twelve kinds of apples, the most popular of which is a tart green variety.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"valid-relative-clause-fix-misread"},{"text":"The orchard grows twelve kinds of apples, and the most popular is a tart green variety.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"valid-conjunction-fix-misread"},{"text":"The orchard grows twelve kinds of apples; the most popular is a tart green variety.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"valid-semicolon-fix-misread"},{"text":"The orchard grows twelve kinds of apples, the most popular one is a tart green variety.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The orchard grows twelve kinds of apples, the most popular one is a tart green variety.$q$, $q$Adding "one" changes a word but still joins two independent clauses with only a comma, so the comma splice remains. "The most popular of which" turns the second part into a dependent relative clause, which is a valid fix.$q$, 'draft', null)
