   $q$Which sentence should replace sentence 2 so that the draft states a clear claim its evidence supports?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Every city in the country should plant a tree on every block before next summer begins.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-analysis"},{"text":"Okafor's study shows that street trees lower the heat people feel and that a lack of shade falls hardest on certain neighborhoods.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Okafor's article is about sidewalks, trees and temperatures in a city called Millbrook during one summer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"},{"text":"Concrete absorbs sunlight during the day and slowly releases that heat during the night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Okafor's study shows that street trees lower the heat people feel and that a lack of shade falls hardest on certain neighborhoods.$q$, $q$Sentences 3 through 10 describe how shade cools sidewalks and how shade is unevenly shared, so the claim about both ideas fits the evidence. The choice about the article's subject only names a topic and makes no point that evidence could prove.$q$, 'draft', '841f2565-2642-504f-afaa-fce168dbd8e2')
