   $q$Which revision of sentence 11 would best conclude the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"From a manager's logbook to a flood rescue, Asante's evidence shows that Larkfield trusted its teenage operators with work that truly mattered.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Teenagers were the only reason that the town of Larkfield survived at all during the nineteenth century.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Today, people send messages by phone instead, which is much faster than using a telegraph.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-detail"},{"text":"Hattie Brennan stayed at her station for two full days during the spring flood of 1874 in Larkfield.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-without-analysis"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$From a manager's logbook to a flood rescue, Asante's evidence shows that Larkfield trusted its teenage operators with work that truly mattered.$q$, $q$The best conclusion links both pieces of evidence back to the claim about trust and responsibility. The choice saying teenagers were the only reason the town survived exaggerates far beyond Asante's evidence.$q$, 'draft', 'ca6d2cdb-7b02-594e-b9ce-ffad53a7f469')
