   $q$Which sentence should replace sentence 2 so that the draft begins with a claim its evidence supports?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Kobayashi's report describes an experiment that took place at a high school called Ridgeview.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"},{"text":"Kobayashi's experiment suggests that a phone can weaken reading focus even when it stays silent on the desk.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Phones should be banned from every school in the country starting next year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-analysis"},{"text":"Science articles are often harder to read than stories because they use technical words.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-generalization"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Kobayashi's experiment suggests that a phone can weaken reading focus even when it stays silent on the desk.$q$, $q$Both the test scores and the interviews support the idea that a silent phone still distracts, so this claim fits. The choice about banning phones is a policy opinion the experiment does not test.$q$, 'draft', '42e9e6fb-6d67-5df5-9790-4d353b6e41c8')
