-- Passage wg10-writing-with-evidence-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('be021c9d-19ba-5312-9674-c15646472be0', 'wg10-writing-with-evidence-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Draft: Dark Towers, Safe Birds$q$, $q$(1) In his article "Lights Out for the Flyway," ornithologist Rafael Moreno examines a program in the city of Port Winslow that asks office towers to switch off their lights after eleven at night during bird migration season. (2) Moreno explains that many songbirds migrate at night and use the stars to find their way. (3) Bright windows can confuse these birds, drawing them toward buildings where they circle until they are exhausted or strike the glass. (4) ____, the program targets the exact hours and weeks when birds are most at risk.

(5) The results Moreno reports are striking. (6) Before the program, volunteers walking downtown each morning found an average of 31 injured or stunned birds per week during migration. (7) In the first two seasons with the lights off, that number fell to 9. (8) Moreno adds that one building manager joked that the dark tower "finally looks like it is getting some sleep." (9) Moreno also notes that the volunteers used the same routes and the same start time every morning, both before and after the program began.

(10) Moreno's evidence shows that a simple, inexpensive change can protect birds.$q$, 'draft')
