-- Passage wg10-writing-with-evidence-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('5ed646ac-f522-5ec4-9ea2-1669a5d10f19', 'wg10-writing-with-evidence-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Draft: A Quilt Full of People$q$, $q$(1) In Leilani Kahale's poem "Patchwork," the speaker describes a quilt her grandmother sewed from the family's old clothing. (2) The poem has four stanzas and does not rhyme. (3) In the first stanza, the speaker notices "my father's blue work shirt, / cut into a square no bigger than my hand." (4) By naming whose clothing each patch came from, the speaker shows that the quilt holds pieces of people, not just pieces of fabric. (5) Later, she points to "the yellow of a dress my aunt outgrew / the summer she learned to swim," which connects a scrap of cloth to a single family memory.

(6) The final stanza shifts from looking at the quilt to using it. (7) On a cold night, the speaker wraps the quilt around her shoulders and says she is "wearing the whole family at once." (8) This image suggests that the memories stitched into the quilt can still comfort the speaker in the present. (9) ____, the poem presents the quilt as a way for a family's past to stay close and useful. (10) My own grandmother knits scarves for everyone in our family every winter.

(11) Kahale is a good poet.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
where public.passages.status = 'draft';
