   $q$Which revision of sentence 11 would best conclude the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Quilts are a popular craft in many countries, and some are displayed in museums.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-generalization"},{"text":"Kahale must have had a very close family, since she wrote a whole poem about a quilt.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The poem \"Patchwork\" was written by Leilani Kahale and has four stanzas that do not rhyme.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"summary-not-conclusion"},{"text":"From the father's shirt to the speaker \"wearing the whole family,\" Kahale turns a quilt into a lasting home for family memories.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$From the father's shirt to the speaker "wearing the whole family," Kahale turns a quilt into a lasting home for family memories.$q$, $q$The best conclusion recalls key evidence and restates the claim about memory. The choice about Kahale's own family assumes the speaker is the poet, which the draft never establishes.$q$, 'draft', '5ed646ac-f522-5ec4-9ea2-1669a5d10f19')
