  ('6aa64682-07f9-541a-8249-02722f989405', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'hard',
   $q$A reader objects that the recess-first schools might simply have served tastier food. Which detail from Mehta's article, if added, would best answer this objection?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The study took place over an entire school year rather than just a few weeks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"does-not-address-objection"},{"text":"Mehta has written several popular books about healthy eating for families.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"appeal-to-authority"},{"text":"All four schools served the same menu each day, prepared in the same county kitchen.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Students at all four schools were allowed to bring lunch from home if they wished.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"does-not-address-objection"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$All four schools served the same menu each day, prepared in the same county kitchen.$q$, $q$If every school served identical food, taste cannot explain the difference in waste, so the schedule becomes the likely cause. The study's length is a strength, but it does nothing to rule out differences in the food.$q$, 'draft', '2c3ba757-29e3-50d1-9750-e68f0936d7e4')
