  ('c0d3078a-ef15-59cc-b010-d3ebb557dc8a', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'hard',
   $q$In sentence 5, why is it important that the writer says "Mehta suggests" instead of stating the explanation as a plain fact?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The explanation is Mehta's interpretation of the data, not something the tray weights measured directly, so it should be credited to him.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Using a researcher's name in every sentence is required in any essay that uses evidence.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralized-rule"},{"text":"Mehta did not take part in the study himself, so the writer is showing that he disagrees with it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-passage"},{"text":"The phrase shows that the writer believes the explanation is false and wants readers to doubt it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The explanation is Mehta's interpretation of the data, not something the tray weights measured directly, so it should be credited to him.$q$, $q$The trays showed how much food was wasted, but the reason why is Mehta's reasoned guess, and attributing it keeps fact and interpretation separate. "Suggests" signals a careful claim, not disagreement or doubt.$q$, 'draft', '2c3ba757-29e3-50d1-9750-e68f0936d7e4')
