  ('126e27dc-20e2-54d9-9d66-8e29966c9ca0', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The draft needs a claim that matches the second paragraph. Which sentence, added after sentence 1, would work best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Haddad's account describes the gutters and storage tanks that were installed on 400 homes in 2018.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"},{"text":"Haddad's account proves that engineers are the most important workers in any small town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Haddad's account shows that Sela Verde's tanks succeeded because the town paired repairable equipment with training for the families who used it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Haddad's account shows that Sela Verde receives far more rain each year than most other towns.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-passage"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Haddad's account shows that Sela Verde's tanks succeeded because the town paired repairable equipment with training for the families who used it.$q$, $q$Paragraph 2 gives two reasons for success, local repairs and cleaning workshops, so the claim naming both fits. The choice about the 400 homes restates a detail from sentence 3 instead of making an arguable point.$q$, 'draft', '3c35cde6-c7ef-58c9-a379-4f3795d988df')
