   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence (2) as the writer's claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Every old building in Kessington must be saved, no matter what it costs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstated-claim"},{"text":"The Harlow Street Depot was built of brick in the year 1911.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fact-not-claim"},{"text":"Old buildings are interesting, and some are more interesting than others.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-wording"},{"text":"The county should restore the Harlow Street Depot as a museum and community hall rather than allow its demolition.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The county should restore the Harlow Street Depot as a museum and community hall rather than allow its demolition.$q$, $q$The correct choice takes a clear, arguable position that the rest of the essay supports. The date of construction is a fact, not a claim anyone could argue against.$q$, 'draft', '69d75746-53fe-5b5e-9e31-a8ecdacb15e9')
