  ('11bd10e1-f409-5172-8238-fdf318c0b2f7', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-argument-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which statement best explains why sentence (7) strengthens rather than weakens the argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"By granting that the housing need is real, the writer appears fair and sets up the solution in sentence (8) that meets that need without demolition.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It adds a statistic showing how many families in Kessington need housing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"invents-evidence"},{"text":"It proves that housing is more important to the town than history.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-purpose"},{"text":"It shows that the writer agrees the depot should be replaced with apartments.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-concession"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By granting that the housing need is real, the writer appears fair and sets up the solution in sentence (8) that meets that need without demolition.$q$, $q$Acknowledging a valid opposing point builds credibility and prepares the reader for a solution that satisfies both sides. Sentence (7) contains no statistic, so the last choice describes evidence that is not in the text.$q$, 'draft', '69d75746-53fe-5b5e-9e31-a8ecdacb15e9')
