  ('be7a9ed2-eea8-5142-98b9-7cf622d8537b', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-argument-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$A reader objects that sentence (5) claims savings without support. Which revision best develops it with reasoning and evidence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Shielded lights would save the town millions of dollars every single year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstated-claim"},{"text":"Saving money is always good for a town and for the people who live there.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"Because shielded fixtures aim all their light downward, a lower-wattage bulb can light the same street, and Corrigan cut its streetlight energy use by about a fifth after switching.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Electricity bills in Marrow Bay are very, very high for everyone in town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-assertion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because shielded fixtures aim all their light downward, a lower-wattage bulb can light the same street, and Corrigan cut its streetlight energy use by about a fifth after switching.$q$, $q$The correct revision explains why shielding saves energy and adds a measured result from a comparable town. The claim of millions saved each year is a large figure with no source.$q$, 'draft', '78c7f5e9-36b1-5db0-a259-60496079ef53')
