   $q$Which change would most improve the fairness and thoroughness of the response to the cost objection in sentences (10) and (11)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Add that residents worried about cost care more about money than about the town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dismissive-tone"},{"text":"Place sentence (11) before sentence (10) so the answer comes before the objection.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"illogical-order"},{"text":"Acknowledge that replacement costs are real for some owners before explaining that the rule applies only to new or replaced lights.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Remove sentence (10) so that readers do not think about the cost of new lights.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"suppresses-counterclaim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Acknowledge that replacement costs are real for some owners before explaining that the rule applies only to new or replaced lights.$q$, $q$The safety objection receives a concession in sentence (7), but the cost objection does not, so adding one makes the treatment fair and complete. Removing sentence (10) would hide an opposing view instead of answering it.$q$, 'draft', '78c7f5e9-36b1-5db0-a259-60496079ef53')
